WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.550
- [Drew] Please welcome the man

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:06.550
behind Brooklyn Banana
Bread Company, Sean Reynold.

00:00:06.588 --> 00:00:07.979
- [Ross] Hi, Sean.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:09.653
- Hi, Drew. Hi.

00:00:09.653 --> 00:00:10.486
Hi, Ross.

00:00:10.486 --> 00:00:11.840
- Hi.
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.573
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.253
As you can see,

00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:17.150
I brought some of that
Brooklyn Banana Bread for you.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.310
- Which I am not gonna lie,

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.110
all I wanna do is ask you a question

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.850
and hear your answer as I chew

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.270
because I've been waiting to try it.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.950
Reading your story was so moving.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.490
And will you tell us
about bringing the bread

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.420
to your girlfriend and
kind of the origin story?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.320
- Okay, so during the height
of COVID, my girlfriend,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.550
she's a nurse, and I
was hearing the story.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.870
She would call me crying, stressed.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.640
So I figured what can I do to
uplift her and her colleagues?

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.440
So I decided to bake my
mother's delicious banana bread.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.250
And I went up there and gave
her unit some banana bread.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.047
And then I started thinking,

00:00:55.047 --> 00:00:56.670
"Well, she has friends and colleagues

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.820
who are healthcare professionals

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.290
and work at other hospitals,

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.570
why not donate to those
other units as well?"

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.047
And then I took it a
step further and said,

00:01:05.047 --> 00:01:06.030
"Hey, you know what?

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.020
Let me donate to every
hospital in New York City."

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.420
- [Ross] Wow.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.995
Wow.
(audience applauding)

00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:14.828
Come on, Sean.

00:01:14.828 --> 00:01:16.787
(audience applauding)

00:01:16.787 --> 00:01:18.210
And how's that journey going

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.860
delivering to every hospital in New York?

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.350
- It's going great.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.350
I mean, I've done almost
every one except for four.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.500
But I've done hospitals in Connecticut,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.470
New Jersey, Delaware, Maryland.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.931
She and I, we even took a trip...

00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:34.540
(audience applauding)

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.040
We took a trip down to
the George Floyd Memorial

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.810
and gave out some there, gave out some

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:41.780
to a food distribution center
out there in Minneapolis.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:45.210
So I'm just having a great time

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.950
showing love and appreciation

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.450
to those who help take care
of us during this time.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.420
- Oh, come on, that is the goal.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.900
That's the reason.
- How are you like this?

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.020
Where does this kindness,
this generosity, this energy,

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.520
where does it come from?

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.090
- So I grew up in a Christian household

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:10.890
where there were values and
principles instilled in me.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.830
Some of those values were working hard,

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.370
being a good financial steward,

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.040
showing love and giving back.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.820
And my mother really embodied
that loving and giving back.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.430
Her generosity showed.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.070
So that's part of my DNA.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.470
So now I just work hard
at loving and giving back.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.381
- [Ross] Ah.

00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:32.340
(audience applauding)

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.470
That is so great and I love it.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.960
It's your mom's spirit in there.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.390
It's also her recipe here.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:41.636
And I know you spent a lot of
money doing this, like 15,000?

00:02:41.636 --> 00:02:42.590
- [Drew] Of your own money?

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:46.323
- Of my own money, over
$15,000 of my own money.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.980
A lot of people out here are hurting

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.303
and it saddens me to know
that they're hurting.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.520
And as long as I have breath in my lungs

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.710
and I have the capacity to do it,

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.760
I will help those individuals that I can.

00:03:05.844 --> 00:03:09.011
(audience applauding)

00:03:10.785 --> 00:03:12.720
- [Drew] I'm so lucky to hear your story.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.680
We're all so lucky to hear your story.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.097
- [Sean] Thank you.

00:03:17.097 --> 00:03:18.187
Thank you.

00:03:18.187 --> 00:03:20.550
- [Drew] What is next for you?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.460
- Well, I'm looking
forward to the next 12,000

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.190
and what would that bring?

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.700
I'm gonna continue
donating, I wanna donate

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.830
and finish up with the
firehouses and the EMT houses

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.270
and the police departments.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.050
- [Drew] And you've got four more to go,

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.270
then where does the mission go?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.947
You put the stamp on, you're like,

00:03:36.947 --> 00:03:39.640
"Okay, I checked all those boxes."

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.260
And then where does your journey take you?

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.560
- [Sean] Well, sometimes
the journey finds me.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.919
I sit back and I have goals for myself

00:03:48.919 --> 00:03:52.480
and for donating, but
sometimes it finds me.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.640
So for me, ultimately, I would love

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.490
to establish a foundation

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.850
where we can start to implant

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.920
these type of donations in every city.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.930
- Well, if you build it, they will come,

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.200
and I appreciate that
life advice to stay open

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.760
to the road that presents itself,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.630
and I appreciate that so much.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.420
And we just admire and appreciate
everything you're doing.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:22.930
And our friends at
Clabber Girl Baking Powder

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.520
appreciate you too, and
they wanna chip in $5,000

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.433
to your ongoing campaign,

00:04:29.437 --> 00:04:32.858
and I'm gonna match it, so that's $10,000.

00:04:32.858 --> 00:04:34.128
- [Ross] Wow.

00:04:34.128 --> 00:04:36.253
- [Drew] Because we love and appreciate

00:04:36.253 --> 00:04:39.610
everything you're doing,
you're the living example,

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.157
and it's the celebration of your mom too.

00:04:43.913 --> 00:04:47.500
- I don't even have words to
explain how I feel right now.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.731
I just thank you, I thank you.

00:04:49.731 --> 00:04:52.210
I thank all of you for allowing me

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.573
to share a story of love and compassion.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.920
And I think that's what
we need in this world.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.500
You do what you can, and
make sure you take care

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.720
of your neighbors.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.553
- [Drew] And you know what?

00:05:04.553 --> 00:05:05.386
Sometimes words are cheap.

00:05:05.386 --> 00:05:08.790
Your action says everything and
may we all be more like you.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:09.923
So how about that?

00:05:09.923 --> 00:05:10.756
- [Ross] Yes please.

00:05:10.756 --> 00:05:12.833
(audience applauding)

00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:13.666
- [Sean] Thank you.

00:05:13.666 --> 00:05:14.675
- [Drew] Thank you so much.

00:05:14.675 --> 00:05:15.577
(audience applauding)

00:05:15.577 --> 00:05:16.740
Thank you for everything that you do.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.380
Thank you, Sean Reynolds.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.010
And if you go to thedrewbarrymoreshow.com,

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:24.370
you'll find all about the
Brooklyn Banana Bread Company

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.970
and how you can support

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.165
and get that yummy banana bread as well.

00:05:28.165 --> 00:05:30.748
(upbeat music)

